"""Archived release notes."""
HISTORY={'0.4': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.24': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.8': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '0.5.1': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.28': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.21': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '0.7': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.23': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '0.6': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.11': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.14': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.9': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.6': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.20': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.7': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.5': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.27': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.18': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.1': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.2': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '0.5': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.17': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.26': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.13': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.29': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.25': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.12': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.15': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.16': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.22': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.3': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.19': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.10': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.4': 'Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.87': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.87\n\nThe installer header now uses a large, proportionally scaled logo mark rather than compressing the wide banner into the header. The location selector and installation flow are unchanged.', '1.0.85': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.85\n\nRestored the standard installer Close button. Show Files now uses the adjacent native button position in the bottom row, outside the completion message. Clicking it opens the installed-file list and leaves the completion page open.', '1.0.69': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.69\n\nOverview reminder and recent bill/deposit entries are plain text. Double-click an entry to open its detail or required assignment action.\n\nThe Penny Pinchers: rebuilt fictional sample\n\nOpen Sample Data loads a fresh household in a separate NestSimpleMoneyDemo-Rebuilt169 folder next to the previous testing folder. The old folder and personal household are preserved. Later launches reuse your edits to this rebuilt sample.\n\nIncludes 2025–October 2026 history, all seven accounts covering every account type, over 1,000 transactions, over 220 bills, 44 contacts, 10 recurring schedules, four goals with payment histories, debt and a completed loan, transfers, reconciliation, attachments, splits, foreign-currency examples, CSV/OFX imports and a restorable backup. Saved currency rates are fictional test values.\n\nUse October 2026 to test red budgets, overdue bills, unassigned receipts and Payday calendar marks on October 30–31. Try the funny contacts, suppliers and addresses. The sample folder contains TESTING-GUIDE.txt, sample-import.csv and sample-import.ofx.', '1.0.32': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.32v1.0.32 — Budget Tracking\n\nThe full spending tracker has progress bars: green within budget, red over budget. Each category shows Budget, Actual, Suggested and Balance. Category details also show these four figures in columns.\n\nEdit budget and Edit actual are on the same line. When several actual records exist, Edit actual opens a selection subpage with Edit selected. A single record opens its editor directly; a paid bill opens its bill editor.\n\nQuick test\n\nOpen Overview, then the spending tracker card.\n\nCheck progress bars and Actual/Suggested figures.\n\nOpen a category with several expenses.\n\nClick Edit actual, select an entry and choose Edit selected.\n\nCancel or save, then use Back.', '1.0.53': 'v1.0.53\n\nAll print pages use PDF layouts. Cards, charts, details and calendars use landscape pages. Long lists continue across full-width pages with repeated headings and page numbers.', '1.0.80': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.80\n\nPrevious and Next icons flank the Bills date field. Supplier dropdown opens wider while its closed control stays compact. New native-sized green/white sort arrows sit directly after header text. Removed Ongoing from Repeats. Existing data is preserved.', '1.0.71': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.71\n\nStraight Previous and Next arrows with hover labels; Bills calendar controls ordered Previous, month field, Next. Removed help beside the main Bills calendar action. Aligned action controls with the left edge of their lists. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.83': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.83\n\nSearch fields clear through a hover-labelled X inside their right edge. Status sorts Overdue, Upcoming, Paid. Bill Details tabs are shorter and scroll internally, and the image explanation is removed. Loan-linked bills show estimated Payments to Go based on the recorded balance and payment amount; link a Loan Account in Bill Entry. Payment sources are Chequing, Savings and Cash. Account Type includes Loan and loan editing exposes Type. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.67': 'v1.0.67\n\nPay Day calendar highlights scheduled income dates in blue in month and year views, including recurring occurrences.', '1.0.63': 'v1.0.63\n\nAccount card titles sit on the page background. Payday bypasses generic date/account list filters; By Account is on the left and recalculates the plan. List shows opening balance and an explicit message when no scheduled items exist.', '1.0.33': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.33v1.0.33\n\nOpen sample data is above the testing message on the main menu.\n\nOverview spending exceptions have red progress bars again.\n\nContact cards no longer resize their wrapping on every layout event.\n\nDelete appears below the contact card on transaction and bill details.\n\nActual and Suggested columns are in category transaction lists, rather than the information summary. Suggested is the category/month suggestion, repeated for reference, not a per-transaction forecast. Actual respects category splits.\n\nQuick test\n\nOpen sample data from the menu.\n\nCheck Overview spending progress bars.\n\nOpen spending tracking, a category, and its transaction list.\n\nCheck Actual and Suggested columns.\n\nOpen a transaction and a bill; check stable contact cards with Delete below.', '1.0.84': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.84\n\nCredit Card is an eligible bill payment source. Mortgage is an account type with debt balances, loan payment planning, remaining-payment support and existing debt icon styling. Installer View Installed Files and Close now share the same row on the completion page. Existing data is preserved.', '1.0.58': 'v1.0.58\n\nSettings removed from Charts selection. Settings now contains Storage with drive, free space, household data and program size charts, and Household Tools with the existing tool tabs.', '1.0.55': 'v1.0.55\n\nOverview account buttons open on a single click. Bills main page has Back and Close icons returning to Overview. Record lists keep single-click selection and double-click viewing.', '1.0.48': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.48NestSimple Money v1.0.48\n\nOverview printing now opens an exact one-page landscape PDF in the default PDF viewer. Expanded cards include all accounts, every tracked category with budget/actual/balance and progress, individual savings goals with dates and remaining amounts, plus reminder details. Bills and Deposits stays compact. A large pie and complete two-column colour key fill the right side. No browser scaling or pagination is used.\n\nUse Print in the PDF viewer. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.73': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.73\n\nMatching blue straight-arrow icons for calendar Previous and Next. Bill Details actions across the top: Make Bill Payment, Open Original, Edit, Delete. Paid bills retain View Payment. Bill information on the left; Original document and Contact tabs on the right. Existing data is preserved.', '1.0.65': 'v1.0.65\n\nSample households receive two monthly income examples per account for 2025-2026 and recurring 2027 pay schedules, once only. Pay Day filter added to the account dropdown. Personal households are not seeded.', '1.0.40': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.40v1.0.40 — Overview Period and Refresh\n\nOverview tools are beside My Money and its period at the top. The calendar selects a month; Whole Year switches to a same-size graphic of all twelve months and shows annual spending and charts. Click a month in the year graphic to return to monthly Overview.\n\nRefresh App is above Open Sample Data. It redraws current data without closing the window. Sample actions no longer close the existing sample window. Installing program updates still requires closing the running application.\n\nQuick Review\n\nCheck top controls beside My Money and the date.\n\nSelect a month with the calendar icon.\n\nChoose Whole Year; check the picker stays the same size and Overview shows the year.\n\nClick a month to return to monthly Overview.\n\nUse Refresh App and Open Sample Data; check the current window stays open.', '1.0.31': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.31v1.0.31 — Spending Tracker\n\nOverview now shows only over-budget categories in a compact card. Click the card to see every tracked category; select an item and choose View transactions, or double-click, to open its transaction list. Double-click a transaction to open its details. Back returns one level; Close returns to Overview.\n\nGoal charts are centered with titles and matching colour keys.\n\nReview checklist\n\nConfirm v1.0.31 in the title.\n\nCheck Overview: only categories over budget appear in red.\n\nClick the spending card and review all categories.\n\nOpen a category, then a transaction, then use Back twice.\n\nProgram: E:\\Documents\\NestSimple-Money-Windows\\NestSimpleMoney\n\nUpdater staging: E:\\Documents\\NestSimple-Money-Windows\\temp', '1.0.50': 'v1.0.50\n\nBudget printing includes every category, budget, actual, suggestion and balance in one landscape page, with a small budget icon on white.', '1.0.39': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.39v1.0.39 — Compact Data Entry\n\nShared entry dialogs now follow the bill form: compact left-side fields, contact information on its own tab where applicable, and fixed Save/Cancel controls. Dates, amounts and short choices use appropriately short inputs. Addresses and notes have two lines. Long explanations move to help controls. Nested scroll areas are removed.\n\nIncome/expense attachment controls are at the top with document previews on the right, including PDF previews and existing attachments. New entries hide the redundant Type choice; new income entries omit expense splits. Currency rates use saved Settings rates without extra rate/date inputs. Existing entries retain their original exchange rate.\n\nQuick Review\n\nAdd income and an expense; check compact fields and separate contacts.\n\nAttach a document and check its preview on the right.\n\nCheck short dates, amounts and choices in account, loan, schedule and budget editors.\n\nVerify Save and Cancel stay visible.\n\nCheck help controls retain explanations and validation appears within the form.', '1.0.75': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.75\n\nBalanced table-page margins. Date, Status and Repeats columns sized to their contents. Bill Repeats show paid/upcoming/overdue symbols before Monthly or Once. Status shows overdue day counts. Table headers toggle ascending and descending sorting, with numeric amount and natural text sorting. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.77': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.77\n\nRemoved the added icon column. Bill status artwork is drawn inside Repeats followed by a space and the count of earlier matching supplier/category bills. The table is constrained by its container with equal internal padding. Sort arrows are green with white outlines. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.70': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.70\n\nBills actions share one toolbar. Suppliers dropdown replaces account filtering. Calendar uses a compact Overview-style month and year graphic while retaining marked dates, search, schedule entry, and record drill-down. Previous and Next use icon-only controls with hover labels. Existing data is preserved.', '1.0.68': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.68\n\nOverview: individual actionable reminders; eight most recent bills and deposits, including paid bills; balance explicitly shown as assets minus debts, excluding future movements from current balances. Matching Overview print output.\n\nExisting household data is preserved.', '1.0.54': 'v1.0.54\n\nAccounts, Income and Charts print information, pie and bar charts together on one landscape page. Backup and Help no longer has Print.', '1.0.34': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.34v1.0.34 — Realistic Icons\n\nMenus, account types and command artwork use the approved realistic 3D icon style. Calendar launch buttons now use a matching calendar icon. Icon-only buttons show hover text, also available with keyboard focus. Application branding remains unchanged.\n\nQuick test\n\nConfirm v1.0.34 in the title.\n\nCheck main menu and account icons.\n\nAdd or edit a bill: hover over the calendar icon and check Choose date appears.\n\nTab to that button and check keyboard focus help, then Enter to open the calendar.\n\nCheck search, edit, save, delete, attachment, backup and transfer commands.', '1.0.30': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.30 — Reviewbody{max-width:760px;margin:40px auto;font:18px Segoe UI,sans-serif;color:#193c58;line-height:1.6}h1{color:#2463d3}v1.0.30 — Goals Chart\n\nThe goals pie chart is centered in its area. The summary chart is titled Savings Goals — Target Breakdown; individual goals show Savings Goal — Progress. Each label below the chart has a solid square matching its pie slice.\n\nQuick review\n\nStart NestSimple Money and check that the window title says v1.0.30.\n\nOpen Overview → Manage savings goals.\n\nCheck that the chart and title are centered in the right area.\n\nCompare each coloured square below the chart with its slice.\n\nOpen a goal and check its progress chart the same way.\n\nThis update changes only program code. Existing household data and settings remain in place.', '1.0.45': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.45NestSimple Money v1.0.45\n\nInstaller logo banner and matching executable icon.\n\nExplicit native Windows taskbar icons.\n\nWhite information cards and contact cards.\n\nCompact landscape printing with white backgrounds. Overview information and selected chart print side by side.\n\nHousehold records and settings are preserved.', '1.0.60': 'v1.0.60\n\nSettings uses the same chart data as Backup. Payday list removes duplicate period filters and fits its columns without a horizontal scrollbar. Payday includes the standard Income calendar subpage control and matching period button names.', '1.0.37': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.37v1.0.37 — Category Layout Correction\n\nThe added summary list is removed. Month, Budget Type, Budget, Actual, Left and Suggested information is restored below the bold Category heading.\n\nThe existing bottom transaction list now contains Date, Description, Category, Type, Budget, Actual, Left and Suggested. Actual respects split transactions. Left is the running category balance after each record; Budget and Suggested are monthly category figures. Double-click a transaction to view its details.\n\nQuick Review\n\nOpen a budget category.\n\nCheck that the information is below the category name and only one list remains.\n\nCheck the bottom list has the planner columns alongside Date and Description.\n\nDouble-click a row and use Back to return.', '1.0.44': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.44NestSimple Money v1.0.44\n\nThe household title is aligned left and the motivational saying right on the same row. The main banner is shorter. The page subtitle sits directly beneath it with no gap and a lighter section colour.\n\nCheck main sections and detail pages. Household records and settings are preserved.', '1.0.64': 'v1.0.64\n\nPay Day shows only recorded and scheduled income, its source, receiving account, date, amount and status. Bills, outgoings and spending forecasts removed. Calendar and account selection filter incoming money.', '1.0.38': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.38v1.0.38 — Contact Information Tabs\n\nAdd and edit income, expenses, accounts and loans now separate financial details from Contact Information. Contact person, address, phone numbers and email are on the second tab. Contact editing also uses a separate information tab. Bill entry retains its existing tabs and preview layout.\n\nSave stays visible below the tabs and saves all fields together.\n\nQuick Review\n\nAdd income. Check Details and Contact Information tabs.\n\nEnter income details and contact information, then save.\n\nReopen the record and confirm both sets of fields were retained.\n\nRepeat for an expense, account and loan.\n\nCheck bill entry still has fields and preview on its first tab.', '1.0.78': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.78\n\nHeader sort arrow artwork is sized to 80% of the header height, retaining the green fill and white outline. No data or other controls changed.', '1.0.43': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.43NestSimple Money v1.0.43\n\nRemoved the contact-type title and alphabet letter tab from every contact card. Contact names, details and Edit Contact remain available.\n\nCheck a bill, transaction and contact detail page. Existing household records and settings are preserved.', '1.0.66': 'v1.0.66\n\nPay Day calendar shows Month View then Whole Year, with Create Scheduled Income opening the existing schedule editor restricted to income.', '1.0.41': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.41v1.0.41 — Page Colours and Print\n\nRefresh App is removed. Overview uses light tan. Transactions has pastel yellow pages and darker title and table-header bars. The demonstration notice is below the testing/password notice in the main menu, rather than across the page.\n\nNon-entry pages have a printer icon in the title banner, with Print hover text. It opens a local report containing the selected page/tab, current visible table rows and vector charts, then invokes the browser print dialog. You can print or save as PDF. Data-entry subpages and Settings are excluded. Reports are saved beside the program under temp/print-reports.\n\nQuick Review\n\nCheck Overview and Transactions colours.\n\nOpen sample data and check the notice below the testing message.\n\nHover over the printer icon, then print Overview or a transaction list.\n\nCheck tables and charts in print preview.\n\nOpen Add Bill and confirm it has no page Print icon.', '1.0.62': 'v1.0.62\n\nAccounts card captions are larger and bold with page-coloured caption backgrounds. Payday retains its list in a wider right column with date filters suppressed. Its single calendar button uses the Overview month/year picker and recalculates the plan.', '1.0.76': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.76\n\nTables fit their containers, with compact Amount columns sized for 1000000.00 and remaining space prioritised for Supplier. Provider labels renamed Supplier. Bill row markers use matching check/calendar/red-X artwork. Header sorting shows blue up/down icons. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.52': 'v1.0.52\n\nAll budget cards, category figures, pie chart and comparison bars together on one landscape PDF page.', '1.0.51': 'v1.0.51\n\nFixed missing Path import in budget PDF printing. Long lists use the full printable width with flowing tables, repeated headers and no reserved blank card pages.', '1.0.74': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.74\n\nClear beside every Search button removes search text and refreshes results while preserving other filters. Bill Details preview is half its previous width and height; click the preview to open the unchanged original. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.57': 'v1.0.57\n\nBills Back and Close use the standard button appearance, matching other pages. Only their surrounding frame matches the banner background.', '1.0.49': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.49NestSimple Money v1.0.49\n\nAll print buttons on card pages now create single-page landscape PDFs with white backgrounds, full information, tables, progress bars and selected charts. Document previews are included. Long spending-card lists print as a compact table. Overview retains its approved dedicated layout. Print from your PDF viewer.', '1.0.72': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.72\n\nStraight Previous and Next arrows with hover labels. Calendar controls ordered Previous, month field, Next, Month View, Whole Year, Add Schedule on one row. Removed help beside the main Bills calendar action. Aligned controls with their lists. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.81': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.81\n\nCompact triangular navigation icons without button borders. Search/Clear share a responsive layout so Clear remains visible. Removed Suppliers label; closed supplier selectors use Bills green with white text, open lists use black text on white. Existing data is preserved.', '1.0.36': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.36v1.0.36 — Budget Category Details\n\nThe category table uses the planner columns: Category, Type, Budget, Actual, Left, Suggested. The separate Edit Actual buttons are removed. Double-click Actual in the category table, or the Actual field in the budget editor, to edit its source records; Enter also works. Multiple records open a selection page, while a single record opens its editor.\n\nCategory and its item name below the banner are bold and larger. The transaction list retains each entry’s actual amount; category-wide suggestions appear in the category summary rather than as misleading per-transaction figures.\n\nQuick Review\n\nOpen a budget category and compare its columns with the planner.\n\nDouble-click its Actual value.\n\nSelect a record and choose Edit Selected if several entries exist.\n\nOpen Edit Budget, then double-click the Actual field.\n\nConfirm the bold Category heading below the banner.', '1.0.82': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.82\n\nHeaders remain centred, including sorted titles and arrows. Dollar values align right and dates centre. Installer completion appears inside the installer with a View Installed Files control rather than a success popup. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.86': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.86\n\nCalendar controls use one row: Add Schedule, Previous icon, period field, Next icon, All Suppliers, search field, Search. Controls share a common height. Choose a month or the year in the period dropdown. Calendar boxes are smaller. The list fits its container without a horizontal scrollbar. Calendar printing shows the filtered list with the month/year title and excludes controls. Clear X is larger and blue. Search artwork has one handle. Existing data is preserved.', '1.0.79': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.79\n\nRepeats shows Once, Monthly or Yearly with remaining payments. Set a limit in Bill Entry; blank means Ongoing. Paying decreases the count and stops creating bills after the final payment. Existing Repeats artwork is unchanged. Status (Days) shows a coloured square, status text and days (paid: 0; upcoming: days until due; overdue: days late). Header arrows doubled. Month/year controls toggle their label and view. Existing household data is preserved.', '1.0.42': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.42v1.0.42 — Navigation, Statements and Printing\n\nBack and Close use icons only, with hover and keyboard-focus labels. Cancel retains its text.\n\nAccount statements no longer show contact details by default. Show Contact opens the linked contact subpage. Add Expense, Add Deposit, Edit Account and Show Contact share a toolbar below the banner. Leading Account, Category, Provider, Name and Description information is larger and bold on detail pages.\n\nPrint reports preserve card borders, card order, side-by-side card groups and grid columns, rather than flattening all content into a single list. Printing uses landscape layout and preserves account names, tables, charts and attached document previews.\n\nQuick Review\n\nOpen a detail page and hover Back and Close icons.\n\nOpen an account statement; check the top action row and larger Account text.\n\nChoose Show Contact and use Back to return.\n\nPrint Overview and compare card placement and order with the application.', '1.0.35': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.35v1.0.35 — Clearer Titles and Tracking\n\nExpense-tracking cards no longer have View transactions buttons. Double-click the category name, or focus it and press Enter, to view details. Redundant headings below the page banner are removed. Titles capitalize their main words while preserving acronyms and version numbers.\n\nQuick Review\n\nOpen Overview → Spending tracker.\n\nConfirm there are no View transactions buttons on tracking cards.\n\nDouble-click a category name to open its details.\n\nCheck the page title appears once, in the banner.\n\nCheck budget pages retain their fixed summary without a duplicate heading.', '1.0.47': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.47NestSimple Money v1.0.47\n\nOverview printing automatically scales its complete contents onto one landscape Letter page. Testing startup reopens an existing saved sample household without resetting its records. Sample windows remember their selected month.\n\nClose the app before updating. Household records and settings are preserved.', '1.0.46': 'NestSimple Money v1.0.46NestSimple Money v1.0.46\n\nOverview printing now uses the landscape page width: summary across the top, all displayed card information in two columns on the left, a large pie chart on the right with its complete colour key and amounts. White backgrounds and extra pages when needed preserve information without clipping.', '1.0.61': 'v1.0.61\n\nPay Day has only the standard Calendar button; old date/month/year fields removed. Right-hand list has a reserved visible area and fitted columns. Settings main Pie and Bar Charts tab now shares the Backup chart specification.', '1.0.56': 'v1.0.56\n\nBills navigation controls match the title-bar background. Taskbar logo is reapplied after the window appears and set on both native window and class icons. Existing pinned Windows shortcuts may need unpinning and repinning.', '1.0.59': 'v1.0.59\n\nHousehold Tools no longer includes Calendar, Goals, Budget or Payday. Income has Calendar and Pay Day buttons; Payday opens as a subpage with standard Back and Close icons. Income Calendar uses the same calendar subpage flow as Bills.', '1.0.88': 'Testing replaces Open Sample Data above Contacts. New Testing window includes version history, newest first, and the shared Style Guide. Installer uses the approved logo, title and Home Accounting Made Simple. tagline. The guide is installed as project rules for future updates. Existing households are preserved.', '0.1': 'Early Home Money release. Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '0.2': 'Early Home Money release. Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '0.3': 'Early Home Money release. Detailed change notes are not available for this version.', '1.0.89': 'Installer branding now matches the menu arrangement: logo left, NestSimple and Money on two lines beside it, tagline below in larger bold type smaller than the title. Added this arrangement to the Style Guide.', '1.0.90': 'Testing version controls are icon-only: Previous decreases the version and Next increases it. Style Guide uses a two-thirds text and one-third visual-reference split, with scrollable examples and the approved command/account icon catalogue.', '1.0.91': 'Installer pages now share one identical padded branding block: navy background, approved transparent logo left, two-line title beside it, and bold tagline below. Removed the separate completion sidebar artwork. Style Guide updated.', '1.0.92': 'Installer layout repaired: restored native directory and completion pages and native bottom buttons. Progress and completion use left-hand branding, with centred tagline and content to the right. Removed the oversized top banner and whole-page repositioning. Household files and settings preserved.', '1.0.93': 'Installer file-progress and completion now share the same page template, branding bitmap, size, position and content-column geometry. Removed the separate larger finish sidebar to prevent a jump on completion. Added process-layout consistency to the Style Guide. Household data and settings preserved.', '1.0.94': 'Bills main-page printing now prints only its displayed list in the full-width Transactions list-report style. Back, Close, Previous/Next and other page controls are excluded. Installer layout unchanged. Household files and settings preserved.', '1.0.95': 'Applied the approved completion-page screenshot layout to folder selection as well as file progress and completion. All three pages reuse the identical branding bitmap and shared panel geometry, with white right-hand content and native footer buttons. Style Guide updated. Household data and settings preserved.', '1.0.96': 'Installer navy background now extends to the left client edge and header bottom. Right-hand information area is explicitly white, retaining its gutter. Shared layout retained across stages. Disabled installer compression and removed unused startup bitmap extraction to reduce startup work; Windows launch timing requires verification. Household data preserved.', '1.0.97': 'Version History now displays changes as numbered points. Design and style changes include labelled image examples. Installer design changes show the approved screenshot; other design changes show the shared graphical style reference. Archived wording is preserved. Household data and settings preserved.', '1.0.98': 'Installer page backgrounds now extend fully from the header to both client edges. One persistent branding panel uses the exact approved reference artwork on every stage. White information column retains a gutter; native header and footer remain fixed. Removed the redundant overlapping inset background panels. Household data preserved.', '1.0.99': 'Installer window is displayed before staging writes. Branding is raised and repainted after each native page becomes visible, preventing it from being covered during page transitions. Approved reference artwork and white content area retained. Windows startup timing and appearance require verification.', '1.0.100': 'Bills Calendar columns are Date, Description, Amount, Type. Type has a red box for Unpaid, green for Paid, yellow for Upcoming, with a space before its text. Future unpaid bills and scheduled expense payments show Upcoming. Calendar list printing follows the same column order. Installer pages now clip sibling painting to protect the persistent logo panel. Startup timestamps are recorded for diagnosis; Windows appearance and startup timing remain unverified.', '1.0.101': 'Installer information titles are bold with one blank line of space above. Folder selection, file installation and completion retain padded text positions. Added the shared rule: never put text against any edge; leave inner padding on all sides. Household data preserved.', '1.0.102': 'Compared installer startup with v1.0.92-94. Restored standard non-solid zlib compression and removed the diagnostic helper call before window creation. Approved layout, logo and title padding preserved. Timing log now measures only branding staging after the window appears. Windows launch speed remains unmeasured. Household data preserved.', '1.0.103': 'Removed the redundant hidden header-logo extraction and loading during installer GUI initialization. Retained the same dialog resource, approved left branding panel and padded titles. This removes unnecessary startup work; Windows loading speed remains unmeasured. Household data preserved.', '1.0.104': 'Bills print report redesigned in the shared card-and-chart style. Summary cards show Total, Paid, Unpaid and Upcoming amounts. Added a payment-status pie chart and supplier bar chart. Printed records and totals follow the displayed list; all records are preserved on readable continuation pages when needed. Page controls excluded. Installer appearance and startup code unchanged.', '1.0.105': 'Choose Install Location: reduced the unused space above the folder field, moved the path and Browse controls up, and raised the required/available disk-space text to keep it visible with bottom padding. Other installer pages and startup code unchanged. Household data preserved.', '1.0.106': 'Transactions printing now follows the Bills card-and-chart layout in the Transactions colour theme. Added Income, Expenses, Net Income and Total Activity summary cards, an income/expense pie and spending-category bars. All displayed transactions print with continuation headings when needed. Installer unchanged apart from version labels. Household data preserved.', '1.0.107': 'Income Calendar and Bills Calendar now print the shared summary-card, pie-chart, bar-chart and complete-list layout. Reports honour the displayed month/year, supplier/account and search filters. Added one-time fictional statement activity for appliance loan, car loan and Visa: repayments, Visa purchases and appliance warranty instalments. Existing testing edits retained; personal households excluded. Installer unchanged apart from version labels.', '1.0.108': 'Income and Bills calendars now have a By Month/By Year toggle immediately after Add Schedule. Date/period fields are plain editable inputs without dropdowns. Previous/Next and printed reports follow the selected month or year. Household data preserved.', '1.0.109': 'Traced installer startup through first-page drawing and the later installation section. Embedded the approved branding bitmap in the EXE, removing startup staging directory creation, bitmap extraction/read-back and timing-log writes. Staging is created only after Install is selected. Cached font/DPI conversion replaces repeated control-layout allocations. Kept integrity checks, approved geometry and personal data. Actual Windows cold-start speed remains unmeasured.', '1.0.110': 'Installer startup comparison build: branding stored as an 8-bit indexed bitmap instead of 24-bit RGB, reducing its size while retaining 196 by 245 pixels and the same display geometry. Startup logic and approved layout unchanged. Test first-launch speed against v1.0.109; no speed improvement is claimed without Windows measurement. Household data preserved.', '1.0.111': 'Fresh installer build for Windows startup recording. Same compact embedded branding image, layout and startup logic as v1.0.110; version labels and release notes updated. This provides a new executable for testing, not a confirmed startup-speed fix. Household data preserved.', '1.0.112': 'Added Install Update directly below Testing. Select a .nsmupdate package, review its version, apply with a program backup, close all registered app windows and restart the current household. Packages contain data and program files; the runner is copied from the installed updater. Paths, hashes and current-file compatibility are checked; failed replacement restores previous program files. Household databases and profiles are excluded. Rebuilt Budget Main, Income, Savings, Expenses and Charts print reports with page-specific summary cards, pie/bar charts and complete category tables. Larger lists continue at readable sizes.', '1.0.113': 'Connected Install Update to the NestSimple Money GitHub update repository. Show the latest version and numbered changes; download and check packages before the existing installation review. Keep Choose Update File for downloaded packages. Household data, settings and program backups are preserved.', '1.0.114': 'Placed Testing and Update side by side above Contacts, with equal widths aligned to the main menu. Renamed the Install Update menu button to Update; its update functionality is unchanged.', '1.0.115': 'Fixed the Budget Savings card to show planned savings instead of hiding its two budget plans behind a zero recorded amount. Added recorded savings, left to save and each category amount to the Savings card. Added six months of savings plan history, and improved Main and Savings print reports with planned-versus-recorded values and the savings history. Existing financial records are unchanged.', '1.0.116': 'Budget header and Savings section header now show planned savings, matching the Savings card. Added source and deposit counts plus leading income sources to Income; available budget, amount left, over-budget count and category count to Expenses; income, planned savings, balance and category count to Charts. Made the Budget Income source list taller, showing twelve rows instead of five.', '1.0.117': 'Removed the Transactions help button and kept its action commands on one row. Combined Income Calendar, Pay Day, Add Income, Edit, Delete and Export actions into one row. Added Overview-style white Income cards for received income, deposits, source count and largest deposit. Cards follow the displayed month/year, account and search filters.', '1.0.118': 'Aligned Income and Transactions action buttons with the left edge of their record tables. Removed horizontal scrollbars from Income and Transactions tables; columns continue to resize within the table. Single-row action buttons switch to icons with hover labels on narrower pages, avoiding horizontal growth. Income cards wrap within their available width. Added the style-guide rule: fit tables, fields and cards to the available width without horizontal scrollbars, and align action rows with their tables.', '1.0.119': '1. Standardized main-page information cards on the Income design: white bordered cards, padded content, bold section-coloured titles, blue totals and wrapping supporting text. 2. Updated Overview, Accounts and Budget cards while preserving their information, navigation and financial calculations. 3. Aligned main-page action rows and summary cards with their associated table content and recorded the common card style.', '1.0.120': '1. Removed slice outlines from all on-screen pie charts. 2. Removed pie-slice strokes from PDF and HTML print reports; colours and labels are unchanged.', '1.0.121': '1. Made all notebook tabs the same height as the selected tab across the application, preserving section colours and navigation.', '1.0.122': '1. Replaced nested Pie & Bar Charts tabs with separate Pie Chart and Bar Chart tabs alongside Manage, including Goals. 2. Added labelled six-month Income/Expenses and planned/recorded Savings trend graphs to the corresponding print reports, preserving their detail tables.', '1.0.123': '1. Added 12-month Income/Expenses and planned/recorded Savings Trend Graph tabs beside Pie Chart and Bar Chart. 2. Extended trend reports and savings history to 12 months, retaining readable history tables. 3. Filled blank fictional sample contact details, including account contacts, once only; preserved existing values and personal households.', '1.0.124': '1. Repaired sample-household startup by including the missing sample_contacts.py module. 2. Sample-window startup now uses the existing visible error handler and startup log. 3. Repair replaces only validated program files, backs up previous versions and preserves household databases, attachments, profiles and testing edits.', '1.0.125': '1. Corrected repair compatibility for the older sample_contacts.py module that lacks complete_sample_fields. 2. Sample-window startup now uses the existing visible error handler and startup log. 3. Repair replaces only validated program files, backs up previous versions and preserves household databases, attachments, profiles and testing edits.', '1.0.126': '1. Removed question-mark help buttons throughout Settings, including its nested and lazily opened tabs. 2. Preserved Settings actions, the Help tab and help buttons outside Settings.', '1.0.127': '1. Added Payment Status pie and Bills by Supplier bar graphs above the Bills main-page table. 2. Graphs follow the displayed bill records and filters, use borderless pie slices and stack at narrow widths. 3. Existing bill actions and print report remain available.', '1.0.128': '1. Restored Total, Paid, Unpaid and Upcoming summary cards above the Bills main-page table. 2. Moved Bills graphs into the sibling Pie Chart and Bar Chart tabs. 3. Cards and graphs follow displayed bill records and list filters.', '1.0.129': '1. Added the missing 12-month Trend Graph tab to Bills beside Pie Chart and Bar Chart. 2. Used contrasting green, red and gold Bills pie slices and matching legends. 3. Cards and graphs follow displayed bill records and list filters.', '1.0.130': '1. Bills Trend Graph now separates Paid (green), Unpaid (red) and Upcoming (gold). 2. Replaced the monthly totals list under the Bills graph with bill names, due dates, amounts and matching status colour boxes. 3. Single-click selects a bill; double-click opens that bill detail. Existing filters and main-page cards are preserved.', '1.0.131': '1. Bills trend includes future bill due dates in its 12-month window and shows Paid, Unpaid and Upcoming dollar totals in the legend. 2. Restored compact one-line bill rows ordered Name, Date, Amount, Status, with status colour boxes on the right. 3. Kept single-click selection and double-click bill details; preserved existing records and filters.', '1.0.132': '1. Bills Trend Graph list headings Name, Date, Amount and Status now sort their columns; repeated clicks reverse the order. 2. Added a green direction indicator and preserved sorting across redraws and filter changes. Bill double-click details remain available.', '1.0.133': '1. Matched list-filter control heights and search clear-X space; added Previous/Next arrows beside date fields. 2. Removed question-mark help controls throughout the app; retained Help navigation and guides. 3. Reduced Accounts card height and let its table fill the remaining page without an outer page scrollbar. 4. Aligned Income actions with table content across main, Pay Day, Calendar and Budget Income lists; updated the style guide.', '1.0.134': '1. Kept Overview card titles coloured and changed all remaining page text and totals to black. 2. Made My Accounts buttons fill the card width with equal space on both sides.', '1.0.135': '1. Added download percentage and byte progress on the Download Update page. 2. Kept the download page open until download and package validation succeed; failures remain on the page for retry. 3. Disabled competing update controls during download and retained checksum, compatibility, backup and rollback checks.', '1.0.136': '1. Unified installed version in personal and sample window titles. 2. Made shared list period filters explicitly show All Dates, Month or Year. 3. Aligned workspace action rows with table content, preserving Bills graph table.', '1.0.137': '1. Placed Bills trend legend in one row of white cards ordered Paid, Upcoming, Unpaid. 2. Added matching coloured squares and spacing before legend titles; preserved totals, graph and bill list behaviour.', '1.0.138': '1. Bills graph initially sorts Unpaid, Upcoming, Paid. 2. Remembers subsequent heading sort choices across redraws, navigation and app restarts.', '1.0.139': '1. Standardized shared summary-card styling and removed the fixed Income card height; cards fit their content and remain equal within each row. 2. Preserved compact Accounts cards, Overview colours, card information and actions, both calendar styles and the Bills graph table.', '1.0.140': '1. Changed the update download progress bar to medium blue.', '1.0.141': '1. Moved Account, Loan, Mortgage, Contact and Transaction entry/edit forms into section subpages with shared Save, Cancel, Back and Close controls. 2. Preserved shared list period/account/supplier/search filters, sorting, selected records and scroll position when returning from details. 3. Distinguished No Records Entered from No Records Match These Filters and added Clear Filters for filtered empty lists. 4. Preserved the Bills graph table, both calendar styles, financial records and attachments.', '1.0.142': '1. Shortened the contact-detail Linked Records list to four visible rows, retaining scrolling and record navigation. 2. Check Statement opens a section subpage with the first Chequing account automatically selected. 3. Accounts first action row: Add Account, Edit Account, Transfer Money, Transfer History and Add Loan; remaining commands are on the second row.', '1.0.143': '1. Transfer Money opens an Accounts entry subpage with Save, Cancel, Back and Close. 2. Transfer History opens an Accounts subpage; edit, delete and double-click transfer details remain available.', '1.0.144': '1. Enlarged every Memo entry field from two to five lines and increased its width, with word wrapping and a vertical scrollbar.', '1.0.145': '1. Back and Close navigation icons and their containers blend into their surrounding subtitle or page background.', '1.0.146': '1. Fixed a Bill Entry import left incompatible with the shared form factory.\n2. Shared record lists show their active period, account or supplier, search and displayed record count.\n3. Capture shared list filters, sorting, selection and scroll position before destroying the list when navigating.\n4. Unpaid sorts with Overdue before Upcoming and Paid; bills due today show red Unpaid consistently with the charts.\n5. Shared main lists resize without horizontal scrollbars; translated empty-result messages and Clear Filters retain existing behaviour.\n6. Preserved the Bills graph table and both calendar styles.', '1.0.147': '1. Changed all closed dropdown fields to light blue with black text, including Bills supplier selectors.\n2. Preserved opened dropdown list backgrounds and selection colours.', '1.0.148': '1. Changed closed dropdown backgrounds to the active section colour, using its light tint and black text.\n2. Preserved opened dropdown lists, selection colours and disabled appearance.', '1.0.149': '1. Accounts, Income and Transactions main reports use the displayed records, active filters and current list order for their details and totals.\n2. Standardized white cards, section-coloured headings, black report text and labelled pie/bar charts.\n3. Wrapped long record text at readable sizes and continued complete lists with repeated column headings and page numbers.\n4. Retained a separate 12-month recorded Income history with account/search filters and exact monthly values.\n5. Preserved household data, the Bills graph table and both calendar styles.', '1.0.150': '1. Retained the v1.0.149 Accounts, Income and Transactions report improvements.\n2. Omitted unchanged v1.0.148 files from this package; the corrected updater also skips files already matching the package.\n3. Added bounded retries for temporary access-denied errors during program replacement and settings saves; permanent denials still stop safely.\n4. Verified program backups and replacements; rollback attempts every replaced file and identifies any restoration failures and backup location.\n5. Removed the unconditional restoration-success message and automatic app restart after failed installation.\n6. Included a standalone repair installer to install the corrected updater without opening the app. Household databases, profiles, attachments and testing edits are excluded.', '1.0.151': '1. Retained v1.0.149 reports and v1.0.150 backup, rollback and unchanged-file improvements.\n2. Use Windows ReplaceFileW for existing program and settings files, preserving their Windows permissions and attributes; retain os.replace for new files and non-Windows systems.\n3. Keep a native replacement backup during each Windows replacement and attempt restoration if the API reports a partial failure.\n4. Check every attempted program replacement during rollback, including a failed replacement that may have changed its target.\n5. Show the complete repair error report and include a standalone repair installer for supported v1.0.148 through v1.0.150 and mixed interrupted installations.\n6. Preserve household data, profiles, attachments, testing edits, Bills graph table and calendar styles. Windows execution still requires confirmation on the affected computer.', '1.0.152': '1. Budget reports follow the current page, displayed category/source filters and row order; category reports retain complete filtered transactions with split-specific amounts.\n2. Distinguished planned savings, available funds including rollover, recorded savings and goal reservations; no plans are counted as recorded money.\n3. Added Savings Goals overview, filtered management-list and goal-detail reports, including displayed payment history and opening allocations.\n4. Standardized white cards, section-coloured titles, black body text, labelled charts, readable wrapped rows and continuation pages with repeated headings.\n5. Retained a separate 12-month savings plan/recorded history and trend, labelled All Savings Categories, with all twelve rows on one readable landscape page.\n6. Retained the working Windows replacement fix and preserved household data, testing edits, Bills graph table and both calendar styles.', '1.0.153': '1. Fixed overlapping names, balances and transaction counts in Overview My Accounts by allocating card space from its contents and reserving separate text lines.\n2. Kept Savings Goals clear of the expanded Accounts card, retaining one landscape Overview page and the existing report sections.\n3. Includes v1.0.152 Budget and Savings Goals report improvements and preserves the working Windows replacement helper and household files.', '1.0.154': '1. Fixed silent Apply Update failure by staging the installed file-replacement helper beside the installed updater and verifying both copied files.\n2. Includes v1.0.153 Overview account spacing and Budget/Savings Goals report improvements.\n3. Preserves Windows native file replacement, validation, program backups, rollback and household data.', '1.0.155': '1. Removed redundant Accounts and Reports tabs from Settings Household Tools.\n2. Moved Import into Tools as a command opening the existing statement-import subpage.\n3. Restyled the Tools backup list to match Bills graph rows, with sortable headings, blue selection, search and vertical page scrolling.\n4. Retained v1.0.154 updater dependency staging, Windows replacement, report improvements and household-file preservation.', '1.0.156': '1. Removed the redundant Tools tab; Household Tools opens its contents directly.\n2. Added a sortable Date column showing each automatic backup file date and time.\n3. Grouped backup and recovery commands together, followed by import, display and installation commands, with responsive wrapping.', '1.0.157': '1. Restored Settings Categories: Budget and Income category lists and existing editing commands load correctly again.\n2. Renamed Household Tools to Tools.\n3. Restored Help as the last Settings tab after Categories and Currencies finish loading.', '1.0.158': '1. Redesigned Transfer Money with From and To account cards, existing account icons and a directional arrow.\n2. Added live balances on the transfer date and a before-save balance preview, including correct handling of edited transfers.\n3. Retained validation, five-line memos, shared navigation and Transfer History; the layout stacks at narrow widths.', '1.0.159': '1. Restored Add Bill by including the corrected bill-entry module compatible with the shared form factory.\n2. After saving new records, Income, Transactions, bill and transfer lists refresh by date, most recent first, while retaining filters.\n3. Charts display Date From and Date To beneath titles, using monthly, twelve-month or account coverage as appropriate.\n4. Expense and bill payment forms provide guided category-and-amount split rows with totals and validation; splits feed existing budgets and reports.\n5. Added optional expense Due Date, retained bill Due Date, and added editable payee/supplier dropdowns plus a bill-payment payee selector.\n6. Recurring bills offer Number of Payments or Continuously, retaining existing recurrence and remaining-payment behaviour.', '1.0.160': '1. Moved live transfer guidance to the right of the left-aligned title.\n2. Aligned Save, Cancel and Transfer History with the account cards; renamed the primary command Save.\n3. Made transfer cards and details resize with the window, reduced spacing and removed unnecessary page scrolling at tested window sizes.\n4. Corrected the transfer save refresh reference and retained account previews, memo and validation.', '1.0.161': '1. Editable payee and supplier fields use white backgrounds; supplier filters accept typed names.\n2. Text dropdown lists sort alphabetically while retaining selected values and chronological month/numeric choices.\n3. Charts Date From and Date To have calendar icons; inclusive ranges update chart values and print dates with validation.\n4. New expenses open Transactions after saving and the saved row is selected and revealed when retained filters would hide it; existing household records remain intact.', '1.0.162': '1. Add Expense uses responsive white cards, account artwork and aligned commands matching Transfer Money.\n2. Selecting a second split category fills its empty amount with the remaining CAD balance; typed amounts are preserved.', '1.0.163': '1. Add Expense keeps entry information on the left and Original Image / Split Payment tabs on the right.\n2. Save and Cancel have consistent heights and sit directly below the entry content; transfer commands use the same sizing.\n3. Transfer guidance uses larger right-aligned text beside Transfer Details, with live stage updates preserved.', '1.0.164': '1. Back and Close use raised standard 3D button faces while their surrounding containers retain the page background.\n2. Back uses the larger Previous triangle icon; navigation commands and hover labels are preserved.', '1.0.165': '1. Expense and Income entry share graphical white cards with larger approved icons and attachment previews.\n2. Expense and Income details match their entry pages, retaining contacts, attachments and expense split allocations.\n3. Back, Home and Close use round glossy green, blue and orange-red buttons; Home opens Overview while Back and Close retain their navigation.', '1.0.166': '1. Print commands use larger icon-only controls matching the 48-pixel Back button, retaining hover labels and printing actions.\n2. Added Budget Planner immediately after Manage, with expected monthly income, editable category plans, historical suggestions and a live Left To Plan balance.\n3. Planner drafts save explicitly with validation and rollback, distinguish planned savings from recorded savings, and print the current draft.', '1.0.167': '1. Budget Planner can auto-populate expense drafts from 12 completed months, using available-month averages with a friendly best-guess warning when history is incomplete; fixed costs use the highest month and savings goals are preserved.\n2. Expected income uses recorded Income for the planner month excluding investment accounts and investment income, with a refresh icon.\n3. Planner totals use black-text white cards; the income-to-budget ratio shows excess in red, and the category list uses the Bills graph style with sortable headings and editable amounts.', '1.0.168': '1. Update download progress follows received bytes without rounding up to completion; 100% appears only after the download closes, verification passes and update files are ready.\n2. Show separate downloading, checksum verification and preparation messages; incomplete or damaged packages never report completion.', '1.0.169': '1. Expected Income uses an icon-only refresh command and recorded Income excluding investments.\n2. Budget Planner shows Total Budget, Total Income and Percentage in black-text white cards, without explanatory text below.\n3. Category rows include icons and Type indicators: green covers the highest prior monthly expense, red falls short, grey has no comparison; indicators update with draft amounts.', '1.0.170': '1. Expected Monthly Income restores its saved amount when the planner reopens, including saved zero.\n2. Icon-only graphical refresh reads the current Income statement records and filters, excluding investment accounts and investment income.\n3. Keep (CAD) on the Expected Monthly Income line; category rows use distinct matching artwork and reuse approved existing icons.', '1.0.171': '1. Compact single-row planner toolbar: Monthly Plan first, followed by Expected Monthly Income (CAD), a larger borderless refresh icon, income amount and right-aligned Auto Populate Budget.\n2. Remove numbered headings and the extra toolbar row to give the category list more space; preserve income refresh and saving.', '1.0.172': '1. Add a live Total Remaining card immediately after Total Income in Budget Planner, showing expected income minus the full monthly budget including planned savings.\n2. Retain the compact single-row planner toolbar, graphical Refresh and saved expected income.', '1.0.173': '1. Add Average Actual Spent before Your Plan, showing unrounded split-aware monthly expenses from the previous 12 completed months using available recorded months.\n2. Include the compact planner toolbar and Total Remaining card from v1.0.171–172.', '1.0.174': '1. Use a standalone circular-arrow Refresh icon without a button face and borderless Your Plan fields.\n2. Replace native application messages with white illustrated popups, larger text and keyboard-accessible confirmations.\n3. Auto Budget rounds expense estimates up to the nearest $20; exact multiples and savings goals remain unchanged.', '1.0.175': '1. Refresh and Print use glossy round icon-only controls matching Back and Home, without rectangular button faces.\n2. Single-line entry fields, dropdowns and action buttons share a 48-pixel height; retain borderless planner amounts.', '1.0.176': '1. Use a smaller 40-pixel glossy planner Refresh icon and shorter shared fields and buttons.\n2. Size friendly messages to their content and illustrate Auto Populate with a budget sheet being filled.\n3. After Continue, preview every category with current and proposed amounts and Up, Down or Unchanged indicators before applying to the unsaved draft.', '1.0.177': '1. Auto Populate review now offers Approve And Save, immediately saving the approved category plan and Expected Monthly Income.\n2. Cancel preserves the current draft and saved plan; failed saves retain the previous amounts. Includes compact controls and the all-category Up/Down/Unchanged preview.', '1.0.178': '1. Double-click Budget bar categories, labels or values to edit the budget item without changing the chart artwork.\n2. Budget Pie, Bar and Trend views share Date From and Date To controls; trend records show Source, Actual and Suggested with double-click category editing.\n3. Calendar launch commands use only the approved calendar icon, without a rectangular button face. Budget category and actual-record lists include Source.', '1.0.179': '1. Suggested budgets round up to the next $10 then add $10; preserve historical methods and overrides.\n2. Refresh hover text is Refresh only. Auto Populate review includes category icons and red up triangles, green down triangles and yellow unchanged squares.\n3. Auto Populate explanation offers Don’t Show This Again; approval review always remains available.', '1.0.180': '1. Approval preview headers toggle ascending and descending sorting; amounts and changes sort numerically while preserving category artwork and approval behaviour.\n2. Budget main-page card icons are larger and aligned at the top right.', '1.0.181': '1. Auto Populate approval shows Total Change and a larger instruction card above the list.\n2. Checkboxes and multi-row selection apply only selected budget changes on Save; category icons are larger and sortable headers are preserved.', '1.0.182': '1. Fix Budget tabs failing to load on Python versions before 3.12 by removing incompatible nested f-string quotes.\n2. Retain the shared card compatibility repair, selected-row approval saving and all existing budget styles and calculations.', '1.0.183': '1. Remove the optional Pillow requirement from Budget refresh artwork, category icons, main cards and approval review by shipping ready-sized PNG artwork.\n2. Preserve budget data, calculations, approved icon style and prior compatibility repairs.', '1.0.184': '1. Remove calendar hover text and default chart From/To ranges to the latest year or shorter available history.\n2. Add once-only fictional sample records for five income sources, preserving personal households and existing testing edits.\n3. Move Auto Populate approval into a Budget Planner subpage with sortable selected-row saving and retained drafts.\n4. Show matching large category artwork on the right of budget category edit screens.', '1.0.185': '1. Show historical monthly average actual payments in Budget edit screens and open their source records for editing.\n2. Double-click record lists to edit the clicked record, keeping Planner review selection unchanged.\n3. Add once-only fictional savings transfers and goal contributions to Emergency Fund A and Retirement Savings, without creating expenses.', '1.0.186': '1. Remove vertical gaps between main-menu section buttons.\n2. Use the approved main-menu colours for all pie charts and matching legends on screen and in printed reports.', '1.0.187': '1. Use the brighter 20-colour reference palette for every pie chart and matching legend, clockwise from the top.\n2. Assign colours in slice order and use lighter tints beyond 20 slices to reduce repeats; preserve chart data and layouts.', '1.0.188': '1. Match Budget Trend Graph legends to the Bar Chart with coloured boxes and labels on one line.\n2. Show the month and exact amounts when hovering over Budget trend data points.', '1.0.189': '1. Group Budget pie charts into expandable main categories while preserving totals and records.\n2. Keep verified update readiness and installation review visible on the download page; report review-loading failures.', '1.0.190': '1. Prevent queued progress from delaying update completion and display callback failures with retry controls.\n2. Keep Ready To Install and Apply Update and Restart above supporting review text.\n3. Provide a standalone repair installer for computers whose existing updater cannot reach installation review.', '1.0.191': '1. Group Savings under Banking, Health and Leisure under Family And Personal, and Food and Insurance under Home in Budget pie charts.\n2. Indent expanded subcategory legends while preserving totals, colours, date filters and saved records.', '1.0.192': '1. Keep Ready To Install and Apply Update and Restart above release notes so completion remains visible.\n2. Show 100 percent only after the installation review loads; retain error and retry controls on failure.\n3. Fix Budget trend hover targets after date controls reposition points; show month and exact series amounts.', '1.0.193': '1. Fix Apply Update And Restart failing with pid when a leftover close-request.json exists.\n2. Read only registered process session files; preserve running-window checks, program backups, rollback and household files.\n3. Fix the same session-file error in the standalone repair installer; preserve the approved update interface.', '1.0.194': '1. Apply the approved Banking red, Home yellow, Utilities green, Transport light blue, Family And Personal purple, Giving pink and Other peach Budget colours.\n2. Use the same main groups and indented categories in Budget lists, Planner, Auto Populate review and reports; preserve category records and amounts.\n3. Single-click main pie or bar categories to expand their full category list; retain headings in place and double-click editing on individual bar categories. Internet belongs to Home and Mobile phone to Family And Personal.', '1.0.195': '1. Use white list backgrounds in Budget Planner and Auto Populate, including category group headings.\n2. Keep Auto Populate column headings and Select All fixed above the scrolling records; retain sortable columns, selections and numeric amount sorting. Budget Planner retains its fixed sortable headings.', '1.0.196': '1. Display installation review and Apply Update and Restart below Check Again, Download Update and download progress; keep existing controls in place when the review appears.', '1.0.197': '1. Correct the installed version number and keep download/review controls reachable with vertical scrolling on shorter update pages; preserve additive control order.\n2. Align Auto Populate fixed headers and records using identical pixel column widths, including the checkbox column and scrollbar allowance.\n3. Align Budget Planner headers with editable columns and maintain alignment during resizing and scrolling.\n4. Centre custom list headers over their columns in Bills Trend, Budget Trend and backup lists; preserve sorting, selection and record actions.', '1.0.198': '1. Fix the blank Update page on older installations by avoiding an unsupported scrolling-helper constructor option.\n2. Keep Check Again, Download Update and progress above installation review and Apply Update And Restart.\n3. Add a real Tk regression against the original installed scrolling helper; preserve program backups, rollback and household files.'}

HISTORY['1.0.199']='1. Keep Date From and Date To controls and the selected inclusive range when expanding or collapsing Budget pie and bar categories; retain the shared range on Trend.\n2. Indent expanded bar subcategories by 24 pixels and restore each bar series to its legend colour.\n3. Remove borders around chart date fields while preserving typing, Enter, focus-out validation and calendar selection.'

HISTORY['1.2.00']='1. Request a fresh GitHub update feed so cached release information cannot hide an update.\n2. Keep repair and update status visible through installation and reopening; require a ready receipt from the reopened app before reporting completion.\n3. Save restart diagnostics and show Retry Reopen when startup fails; preserve the chosen household, program backups and rollback.\n4. Include the v1.0.199 chart fixes: retained From/To controls, borderless date fields, indented subcategories and bars matching the legend.'

HISTORY['1.2.01']='1. Simplify the standalone repair to replace six program files directly, with a program backup.\n2. Do not wait for, close or reopen app processes during standalone repair. Preserve household databases, profiles and testing edits.'
